    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "50\nyears\n1947 - 1997\nBeverages\nTE malaysia",
      "WINE\nBORDEAUX RED\nCARRUADES DE LAFITE 1993 PAUILLAC\nMIS EN BOUTEILLE A LA PROPRIÉTA\nCARRUADES DE LAFITE\n1003\nPAUILLAC\nAPPELLATION PAUILLAC CONTRÔLÉE\nSOUTH AFRICAN RED\nALLESVERLOREN CABERNET SAUVIGNON 1989\nAllesverloren\nCABERNET SAUVIGNON\nPROUCI OF THE REPUBUC OF SOUTE AFRICA\nHistory \u0026 Philosophy\nThis wine from the famous Chateau Lafite Rothschild\nis made with the classic Bordeaux varieties of\nCabernet Sauvignon, Cabernet Franc and Merlot.\nIt has a strong ruby colour with aromas of wood\nand red fruits. A fleshy wine with tannins which melt\naway with ageing.\nHistory \u0026 Philosophy\nThis Cabernet Sauvignon is from the historic wine\nfarm of Allesverloren (1704), the only wine estate in\nthe Swartland Wine of Origin district.\nCabernet Sauvignon 1989 is a powerful dark\nruby-garnet wine. It is high in extracts and brimming\nwith opulent fruitiness. Oak-ageing has lent its thread\nof complimentary vanilla spice, sturdy tannins,\nharmonising impeccably balanced fruit acids and\nalcohol will make this wine grow in stature for\nyears to come\nWINE\nSOUTH AUSTRALIAN RED\nTAYLORS CABERNET SAUVIGNON 1990\nTAYLORS\n1990\nCabernet Sauvignon\nCe Can\nAAA\n125% ALONOL\nPRODUCT OF ALSTRALIA\n750 ml\nBURGUNDY WHITE\nCHABLIS 1er CRU 1995 LES VAILLONS\nLABOURÉ ROI\nCHABLIS 1er CRU\nLES VALL\n11% al\n1995 LABCE-ROI 1995\nHistory \u0026 Philosophy\nVintaged from Cabernet Sauvignon grapes grown\nsolely on Taylors Estate Vineyards in the Clare Valley\nof South Australia.\nThe strong varietal aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon\nis evident along with a complexity derived from subtle\noak treatment.\nThis wine has a well structured but elegant style\nwith a soft acid and tannin finish.\nHistory e Philosophy\nMade solely from the Chardonnay grape variety,\nthis wine comes from a district which produces some\nof the most famous of all white Burgundies.\nChablis 1er Cru 1995 Les Vaillons is pale straw in\ncolour with reflections of gold. The bouquet is\ncomplex, powerful and remarkably carthy. On the\npalate, it is very well balanced and easy to drink with\nsoft fruit and adequate acidity."
    ],
